 "beats": [
  {
   "beat": 1,
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 7.652,
   "text": "Leave a pipe full of water out on the street in January, and it freezes solid. Ice takes up about nine percent more space, and it cracks iron."
  },
  {
   "beat": 2,
   "start": 7.757,
   "end": 13.357,
   "text": "So you bury the water main deep. Below the frost line, the ground never freezes, even when it's freezing up top."
  },
  {
   "beat": 3,
   "start": 13.461,
   "end": 20.22,
   "text": "But firefighters need that water up here. So you run a pipe up to the street. Now that pipe is full of water, sitting in the cold air."
  },
  {
   "beat": 4,
   "start": 20.267,
   "end": 24.185,
   "text": "It freezes. And the night there's a fire, your hydrant is a block of ice."
  },
  {
   "beat": 5,
   "start": 24.232,
   "end": 30.284,
   "text": "Here's the trick: move the valve. Put it way down at the bottom, next to the main, as deep as seven feet underground."
  },
  {
   "beat": 6,
   "start": 30.307,
   "end": 37.113,
   "text": "When it's closed, the water stops down there, in the warm ground. The part above the street stays empty. That's a dry barrel hydrant."
  },
  {
   "beat": 7,
   "start": 37.148,
   "end": 44.823,
   "text": "To open it, a long steel rod runs from the valve all the way up to the nut on top. Firefighters turn the nut, the valve opens, and water shoots up."
  },
  {
   "beat": 8,
   "start": 44.846,
   "end": 53.009,
   "text": "But when they shut it, the barrel is still full of water. So there's a tiny drain hole at the bottom. It opens when the valve closes, and the water soaks into the gravel."
  },
  {
   "beat": 9,
   "start": 53.078,
   "end": 54.783,
   "text": "Empty barrel. Nothing to freeze."
  },
  {
   "beat": 10,
   "start": 54.817,
   "end": 61.043,
   "text": "In Florida and Southern California, it never freezes, so hydrants there just stay full. Those are wet barrel hydrants."
  },
  {
   "beat": 11,
   "start": 61.078,
   "end": 64.278,
   "text": "But wait. Why is the nut on top of your hydrant five-sided?"
  }
 ],
